WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.262
Unit 1 is the guide's
Step 1, in four parts.

2
00:00:03.262 --> 00:00:07.163
First, grant the reader its roles:
Reader on each subscription

3
00:00:07.163 --> 00:00:10.375
in scope is enough to see
its Service Health events.

4
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:13.110
But a security advisory's
sensitive fields,

5
00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.213
and its impacted resources, need
Service Health Security Reader.

6
00:00:17.213 --> 00:00:19.650
Reader and Monitoring
Reader can't see them.

7
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:24.212
Second, sign in in the right cloud,
with the Resource Graph extension.

8
00:00:24.212 --> 00:00:27.598
A GCC agency's subscriptions
are commercial Azure,

9
00:00:27.598 --> 00:00:31.225
the Azure Cloud setting;
Azure Government uses its own.

10
00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:36.637
Third, collect, with the kit's events
query and Learn's impacted-resources query.

11
00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:39.928
And fourth, alert at scale:
plan the built-in policy

12
00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:43.138
at the management group,
with a remediation task.

13
00:00:43.138 --> 00:00:46.464
The gate passes when every
subscription's events are

14
00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:49.638
listed and each security
advisory has its summary.

15
00:00:49.638 --> 00:00:53.710
An empty summary is the sign that
the reader lacks the elevated role.
